1
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,897
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:21,120
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:24,937
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:27,667
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:37,497
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:40,897
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you!

7
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:43,577
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:46,657
So bright, so bold, and so elusive.

9
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,737
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,877
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,960 --> 00:00:55,697
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:58,020
I'm really, really stuck on you.

13
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem!

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,577
Then I won't stop till I
get there, you will see.

15
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:08,897
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:12,100
We'll live in wonderland.

17
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:21,097
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,180 --> 00:01:24,157
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,557
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,937
We'll live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,020 --> 00:01:32,037
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,537
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:36,617
But we don't wanna live ordinary life.

24
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:39,777
But we have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:42,680
We live in one another.

26
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:09,660
What's wrong, huh?

27
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:12,717
You've had that brooding look
on your face for a while.

28
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:15,800
Yeah, I guess I hoped I
was dreaming. About what?

29
00:02:16,080 --> 00:02:19,677
This may sound crazy, but it
seems to me we're not even moving.

30
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:20,590
You feel that?

31
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:31,146
Now that you mention it, the sail doesn't
appear to be catching any wind at all.

32
00:02:34,620 --> 00:02:36,197
No! We're screwed!

33
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:37,597
We've entered the Calm Belt!

34
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:39,440
The Clam Belt? What's that?

35
00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:40,497
Calm Belt!

36
00:02:40,580 --> 00:02:42,797
A part of the sea where
nothing moves a muscle!

37
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:45,040
So there's muscles and clams? No!

38
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:52,446
What was that, an earthquake?

39
00:02:52,780 --> 00:02:54,497
A good trick since we're at sea.

40
00:02:54,580 --> 00:02:56,877
All of this chit-chat isn't
going to get us out of here.

41
00:02:56,960 --> 00:02:58,777
Fold the sails and start paddling now.

42
00:02:58,860 --> 00:03:00,477
We have to get back on course.

43
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:02,780
You can count on me. Don't panic.

44
00:03:02,940 --> 00:03:04,597
And besides, this is a sailboat.

45
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:05,717
Why do we need to paddle?

46
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:06,630
True.

47
00:03:06,713 --> 00:03:07,757
And why would we go through the trouble of

48
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:09,897
doubling back when the
Marines are waiting for us?

49
00:03:09,980 --> 00:03:11,317
Look, there's no time to argue.

50
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:13,017
Just shut up and do as I say.

51
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:15,100
At least it's nice and quiet here.

52
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:16,330
Oh, fine.

53
00:03:16,413 --> 00:03:17,957
If I need to explain it to you, I will.

54
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:19,657
In our haste to escape from the Marines,

55
00:03:19,740 --> 00:03:23,217
we ended up going too far south and now
we're off course and stuck out here!

56
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:24,877
So we entered the Grand Line?

57
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:25,920
Woo-hoo-hoo!

58
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:31,132
If we were at the Grand Line, you think
I'd waste my time explaining this?!

59
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:32,220
Now look!

60
00:03:32,740 --> 00:03:34,777
The Grand Line is sandwiched in the middle

61
00:03:34,860 --> 00:03:36,937
between these two green
areas you see here,

62
00:03:37,020 --> 00:03:37,902
you understand?

63
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:41,837
These areas, just as they're labeled,
are what's called the Calm Belt.

64
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:43,096
That's where we are.

65
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:47,557
Nobody knows why, but inside the Calm
Belt, there's no wind and no current.

66
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:49,997
It's like a void where
everything's stagnant.

67
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:54,457
Given that sailboats move by catching
winds, this is more than a dangerous region.

68
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:55,952
It can be fatal, get it?

69
00:03:56,140 --> 00:03:58,777
Nope, but it sounds like
we're in big trouble.

70
00:03:58,860 --> 00:04:01,177
Good, you retained more
than I thought you would.

71
00:04:01,260 --> 00:04:04,457
So this is what that geezer meant
when he said it was dangerous.

72
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:07,457
Well, that explains why we haven't
gotten a single gust of wind.

73
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:09,917
How are we gonna get out of
this if our ship can't move?

74
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,977
Maybe the wind will start blowing again.

75
00:04:12,060 --> 00:04:14,240
Wind never blows in the calm belt.

76
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:15,497
And that's not all.

77
00:04:15,580 --> 00:04:18,697
There's another good reason that
people call this area dangerous.

78
00:04:18,780 --> 00:04:20,480
It's infested with blood.

79
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,100
What was that?

80
00:04:27,660 --> 00:04:28,780
Sea monsters!

81
00:04:29,380 --> 00:04:30,660
They're gigantic!

82
00:04:36,580 --> 00:04:39,360
The Calm Belt is also
home to the Sea Kings.

83
00:04:39,660 --> 00:04:41,719
It's their main place for breeding.

84
00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:45,349
They're the biggest reason
people can't cross the Calm Belt.

85
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:49,180
Any idea how we get out of this?

86
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:52,337
We don't want to give them any
reason to stick around or eat us.

87
00:04:52,420 --> 00:04:54,337
Once they're gone, we'll paddle back.

88
00:04:54,420 --> 00:04:55,250
Got it?

89
00:04:55,333 --> 00:04:56,315
You call that a plan?

90
00:04:56,940 --> 00:04:57,770
Shut up!

91
00:04:59,980 --> 00:05:00,810
Sorry.

92
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:07,266
That didn't improve anything!

93
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:08,697
It sounds like it's gonna!

94
00:05:08,780 --> 00:05:12,074
Please yourselves, I think
this behemoth's gonna sneeze!

95
00:05:27,700 --> 00:05:30,337
Well, at least we're back
on our original course.

96
00:05:30,420 --> 00:05:34,479
According to the map, we should be
spotting the red line anytime now.

97
00:05:37,620 --> 00:05:40,444
Wow, we're almost there,
the Grand Line at last!

98
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:42,780
Isn't this exciting?

99
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:45,720
We're finally going! We did it! We did it!

100
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:48,500
Cut it out! Sorry.

101
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:50,310
Zoro!

102
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:51,800
You must be right.

103
00:05:52,220 --> 00:05:56,920
Is the path to the Grand Line really as
perilous as it's drawn here? Stop that!

104
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:04,020
Take a look.

105
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:08,831
I'm familiar with the rumors
and these drawings confirm it.

106
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:13,449
As unimaginable as it may seem, the
entrance to the Grand Line is a mountain.

107
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:15,837
So what, did we crash into it?

108
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:17,155
You gotta be kidding.

109
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:19,577
I didn't believe it, but the map's clear.

110
00:06:19,660 --> 00:06:22,037
The mountain appears to be
riddled with small canals,

111
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:24,355
so we might have to go up and over it.

112
00:06:25,440 --> 00:06:26,780
Sounds like fun.

113
00:06:27,460 --> 00:06:28,937
What are you talking about?

114
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:32,917
Even if there are canals or whatever,
a ship can't climb up a mountain.

115
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,706
Well, the map says otherwise.

116
00:06:35,060 --> 00:06:37,757
That's right, and if Nami thinks
something can be done, then it can't.

117
00:06:37,840 --> 00:06:38,670
Got that?

118
00:06:38,753 --> 00:06:42,177
Yeah, but remember, that map was stolen
from Buggy the Clown, so can we trust if...

119
00:06:42,260 --> 00:06:44,017
In case no one noticed,
the rudder's stuck.

120
00:06:44,100 --> 00:06:48,940
A little help over here be nice Sanji,
would you please give Usopp a hand?

121
00:06:49,140 --> 00:06:52,677
I can't think with all his shouting
It's happening right away, Nami!

122
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:53,590
Okay.

123
00:06:54,240 --> 00:06:57,711
Uh, does this current seem
unusually strong to anyone else?

124
00:06:58,660 --> 00:07:00,117
Usopp, what did you just say?

125
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:03,517
I asked if any of you noticed the
insane strength of this current.

126
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:04,430
The current?

127
00:07:04,513 --> 00:07:05,880
That must be... What is it?

128
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:09,120
The canals do go up the
mountain. Oh, come on.

129
00:07:09,240 --> 00:07:10,617
How could that possibly work?

130
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:11,637
Look right here.

131
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:12,550
You see?

132
00:07:12,633 --> 00:07:15,517
The guiding light was directing us
toward this spot on the red line.

133
00:07:15,600 --> 00:07:18,357
Notice how it's labeled
here, Reverse Mountain.

134
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:19,270
Hello?

135
00:07:19,353 --> 00:07:21,121
Little help over here, thank you!

136
00:07:21,280 --> 00:07:24,809
These green lines represent
canals, or artificial waterways.

137
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:28,337
If major currents from all four
oceans flow toward this mountain,

138
00:07:28,420 --> 00:07:30,037
what do you think's gonna happen?

139
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:32,697
The currents would force
water up these canals,

140
00:07:32,780 --> 00:07:36,277
collide at the top, and then flow
straight down into the Grand Line.

141
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:39,157
Now, Reverse Mountain is a winter
mountain, so it's cold, right?

142
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:41,617
That means any surface
currents that don't flow

143
00:07:41,700 --> 00:07:44,237
up the canal will be
forced down as they cool.

144
00:07:44,320 --> 00:07:46,917
Anything riding those currents
would be pulled down as well.

145
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,877
If we screw up and miss
the entrance to the canal,

146
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:51,757
the Going Mary will be
carried straight into

147
00:07:51,840 --> 00:07:54,722
the Red Line's rock base
and likely be destroyed.

148
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:58,037
Ship and crew would be sucked
to the bottom of the sea.

149
00:07:58,120 --> 00:07:58,950
Understand?

150
00:07:59,640 --> 00:08:00,470
Yeah.

151
00:08:00,553 --> 00:08:02,159
Basically, it's a mystery mountain.

152
00:08:04,700 --> 00:08:06,540
No, that's not my point at all.

153
00:08:07,140 --> 00:08:07,970
Anyway,

154
00:08:08,053 --> 00:08:09,477
since we're positioned on this current,

155
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:12,977
we shouldn't run into any problems
getting to the summit of Reverse Mountain.

156
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:15,957
Only thing that would hurt us now is if
something went wrong with the rudder.

157
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:17,640
Nami, you're a genius!

158
00:08:18,180 --> 00:08:21,237
Call me a skeptic, but ships
do not climb mountains.

159
00:08:21,320 --> 00:08:22,937
Well, I've heard a few stories.

160
00:08:23,020 --> 00:08:25,400
Stories about the Mystery Mountain? No,

161
00:08:25,540 --> 00:08:28,297
what I have heard is that more
than half the people who try

162
00:08:28,380 --> 00:08:31,777
to make it to the Grand Line
die before they even get there.

163
00:08:31,860 --> 00:08:34,448
Whatever we find, it
isn't going to be easy.

164
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:36,940
Sanji, could you get the sail?

165
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:40,120
Anything for you, Nami! Luffy, help me!

166
00:08:42,920 --> 00:08:43,880
Got it!

167
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:53,270
Hey!

168
00:08:53,353 --> 00:08:55,160
I can see the mystery mountain!

169
00:08:57,840 --> 00:08:59,580
That's insanely huge!

170
00:09:01,180 --> 00:09:02,877
Wow! Awesome!

171
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:04,780
It's bigger than I thought!

172
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:07,680
I can't see the top!

173
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,220
It's taller than the clouds!

174
00:09:30,940 --> 00:09:33,860
We're getting sucked in!

175
00:09:34,300 --> 00:09:35,940
Hold the rudder steady!

176
00:09:36,640 --> 00:09:37,540
We're on it!

177
00:09:40,220 --> 00:09:41,050
Nami!

178
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:46,287
Where's that entrance
you were talking about?

179
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:50,028
If we keep this heading, we're
going to crash into the rocks!

180
00:09:52,340 --> 00:09:54,160
There's a crack in that cliff.

181
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:55,900
That must be it.

182
00:09:57,260 --> 00:09:58,090
Nami!

183
00:09:58,220 --> 00:09:59,420
Give us a direction!

184
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:01,687
Keep bearing straight ahead!

185
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:03,820
You can't be serious! Trust me!

186
00:10:04,760 --> 00:10:05,817
Have we made it?

187
00:10:05,900 --> 00:10:07,217
Is that the canal entrance?

188
00:10:07,300 --> 00:10:08,300
More than likely.

189
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:10,700
I've got to be dreaming.

190
00:10:11,540 --> 00:10:12,740
It's impossible.

191
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:16,160
The ocean really is
flowing up the mountain.

192
00:10:20,020 --> 00:10:23,177
We have to make our way through
those water gates just right.

193
00:10:23,260 --> 00:10:26,672
Or we'll crash into the red
line and be smashed to pieces.

194
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,677
We're drifting off course.

195
00:10:31,760 --> 00:10:32,917
Gotta go more to the right.

196
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:33,997
Go right.

197
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:35,140
Go in starboard.

198
00:10:37,900 --> 00:10:39,260
Come on, now!

199
00:10:39,380 --> 00:10:40,674
Put your back into it!

200
00:10:47,160 --> 00:10:48,480
The runner!

201
00:10:49,380 --> 00:10:51,700
Gum-Gum balloon!

202
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:01,320
Loopy!

203
00:11:02,180 --> 00:11:03,500
Grab a hold!

204
00:11:15,700 --> 00:11:17,480
We made it!

205
00:11:25,900 --> 00:11:28,580
Now it's just a straight
shot to the summit!

206
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:34,180
Wow, great view!

207
00:11:44,420 --> 00:11:45,250
Whoa!

208
00:11:45,480 --> 00:11:46,780
Look how high we are!

209
00:11:46,900 --> 00:11:48,080
We're in the clouds!

210
00:11:58,540 --> 00:12:00,040
This is insane!

211
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:05,351
We're not in the clouds, we're above them!

212
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:17,137
It's amazing! We've done it!

213
00:12:17,220 --> 00:12:18,691
We've reached the summit!

214
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:32,190
Woohoo!

215
00:12:53,820 --> 00:12:55,840
I can see it!

216
00:12:56,140 --> 00:12:58,697
This is the greatest
sea in the whole world!

217
00:12:58,780 --> 00:13:00,320
The Grand Lie!

218
00:13:02,420 --> 00:13:06,596
Somewhere out there, the One Piece
is waiting, and we're gonna find it!

219
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:08,360
Let's go!

220
00:13:24,420 --> 00:13:26,337
Did you guys just hear something?

221
00:13:26,420 --> 00:13:28,480
It was probably just the wind!

222
00:13:28,760 --> 00:13:31,320
At this speed, everything
sounds distorted!

223
00:13:35,920 --> 00:13:37,140
What was that?

224
00:13:37,820 --> 00:13:38,650
Nami!

225
00:13:38,733 --> 00:13:41,940
I see a mountain up ahead!
What? That's impossible!

226
00:13:42,560 --> 00:13:43,617
But it's right there!

227
00:13:43,700 --> 00:13:44,680
I can see it!

228
00:13:44,780 --> 00:13:46,580
Who cares? Go!

229
00:13:47,640 --> 00:13:51,934
After we pass the twin caves up ahead,
there should be nothing but ocean!

230
00:14:02,560 --> 00:14:03,917
It's a black wall!

231
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:04,857
No, it's not!

232
00:14:04,940 --> 00:14:05,940
Then what is it?

233
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:08,380
It's a whale!

234
00:14:12,780 --> 00:14:14,117
What are we going to do?

235
00:14:14,200 --> 00:14:15,097
Should we fight?

236
00:14:15,180 --> 00:14:17,797
Idiots, how are we supposed
to fight a hundred-ton whale?

237
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:18,740
Do something!

238
00:14:18,980 --> 00:14:20,017
Our path is blocked!

239
00:14:20,100 --> 00:14:22,180
How do we escape? Calm down.

240
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:28,120
If this creature looks like a giant wall
to us, We must be a speck! That's right!

241
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:31,337
It's highly possible that this thing
isn't even aware that we're here!

242
00:14:31,420 --> 00:14:33,957
We'll run right into it
unless we change course!

243
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:34,870
Look!

244
00:14:34,953 --> 00:14:36,249
We can get by on the left!

245
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:37,830
Port!

246
00:14:37,913 --> 00:14:38,920
Port to port!

247
00:14:39,180 --> 00:14:40,400
The rudder's broken!

248
00:14:41,740 --> 00:14:42,570
Do something!

249
00:14:42,653 --> 00:14:46,000
Anything! Wait! I know!
This'll work! It has to!

250
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:48,190
Hey!

251
00:14:48,273 --> 00:14:49,369
Luffy, what are you doing?

252
00:14:56,440 --> 00:14:57,800
This is pointless!

253
00:14:58,060 --> 00:14:59,517
The ship's not going to turn!

254
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:00,430
Dammit!

255
00:15:00,513 --> 00:15:01,343
Don't give up!

256
00:15:10,940 --> 00:15:12,400
Is this the end?

257
00:15:20,280 --> 00:15:21,640
The cannon!

258
00:15:23,140 --> 00:15:23,970
Done.

259
00:15:36,780 --> 00:15:39,360
Hey, that was my special scene!

260
00:15:56,780 --> 00:15:57,610
Damn!

261
00:15:57,693 --> 00:15:58,837
Let's get out of here
before it's too late!

262
00:15:58,920 --> 00:16:00,937
Don't mind telling me
what the heck is going on!

263
00:16:01,020 --> 00:16:03,577
It's so big that the cannonball
didn't even make it flinch!

264
00:16:03,660 --> 00:16:05,377
That or his reaction time's really slow!

265
00:16:05,460 --> 00:16:06,290
Who cares?

266
00:16:06,373 --> 00:16:07,203
At least we're alive!

267
00:16:13,900 --> 00:16:14,730
My ears!

268
00:16:14,813 --> 00:16:15,643
Just battle!

269
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:17,546
I have to get away from here!

270
00:16:23,580 --> 00:16:24,410
Luffy?

271
00:16:24,493 --> 00:16:26,900
You think you can break my special seat?

272
00:16:27,100 --> 00:16:28,220
Get away with it!

273
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:29,880
Take this!

274
00:16:31,820 --> 00:16:32,940
You moron!

275
00:16:41,680 --> 00:16:43,097
I'm not through with you!

276
00:16:43,180 --> 00:16:44,417
There's a lot more with it!

277
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:46,088
Shut up before you kill us!

278
00:16:49,940 --> 00:16:51,340
Please, no!

279
00:17:14,940 --> 00:17:17,760
I am not gonna die!

280
00:17:43,780 --> 00:17:44,637
Oh, man.

281
00:17:44,720 --> 00:17:46,602
Everyone's been swallowed whole.

282
00:17:47,660 --> 00:17:48,560
Hey, you!

283
00:17:48,820 --> 00:17:49,761
Can you hear me?

284
00:17:49,900 --> 00:17:50,730
Spit him out!

285
00:17:50,813 --> 00:17:52,560
I want my friend! Damn you!

286
00:17:53,980 --> 00:17:56,509
Where do you think
you're going, you jerk?!

287
00:17:57,140 --> 00:18:01,780
You give them back right now, you whale!

288
00:18:02,640 --> 00:18:05,440
Listen, you big bone,
I'm not gonna ask again!

289
00:18:05,700 --> 00:18:07,820
Stop sinking, I mean it!

290
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:10,737
My friends and me are on
an important adventure!

291
00:18:10,820 --> 00:18:12,100
I can't lose them!

292
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:13,780
Give them back!

293
00:18:36,880 --> 00:18:43,677
So what do you think I don't know what
to think is this even real because

294
00:18:43,760 --> 00:18:48,054
I know exactly what I saw and what I
felt we were swallowed by the whale?

295
00:18:49,700 --> 00:18:51,120
Is this a dream?

296
00:18:51,700 --> 00:18:53,900
Yeah, I'd say that's a fair guess.

297
00:18:59,460 --> 00:19:03,160
Then what's with this island
and the house? Illusions.

298
00:19:08,580 --> 00:19:10,977
Um, that looks like...

299
00:19:11,060 --> 00:19:13,280
A Great Game Squad!

300
00:19:35,780 --> 00:19:37,460
Looks like someone's home.

301
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:39,440
Let's hope it's a person.

302
00:19:40,060 --> 00:19:41,220
I've had it.

303
00:19:41,460 --> 00:19:42,300
Let's go.

304
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:44,421
Giant squids, guys with harpoons.

305
00:19:44,580 --> 00:19:45,700
And where is Luffy?

306
00:19:46,420 --> 00:19:48,020
Yeah, where is he?

307
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:52,600
I don't know much about whales,

308
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:56,035
but since when do they have
doors and lighted hallways?

309
00:19:58,640 --> 00:19:59,520
A ship?

310
00:20:01,680 --> 00:20:03,840
We should fire a cannon there! Now!

311
00:20:05,380 --> 00:20:06,917
No, hold on a sec.

312
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:08,235
Someone's coming out.

313
00:20:16,660 --> 00:20:21,377
I wrote you a love song
to let you know that

314
00:20:21,460 --> 00:20:25,940
I want to be with you
till the end of time.

315
00:20:27,260 --> 00:20:33,917
Even when the sparkles fade in doubts
invade our ones so trusting might.

316
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:37,480
I promise you that I will stay,

317
00:20:37,700 --> 00:20:43,057
we'll find a way to look
through the cloudy skies.

318
00:20:43,140 --> 00:20:46,277
We built a castle of sand.

319
00:20:46,360 --> 00:20:50,517
And now we're watching it wash away.

320
00:20:50,600 --> 00:20:54,577
It doesn't have to end.

321
00:20:54,660 --> 00:20:56,797
We'll start again.

322
00:20:56,880 --> 00:21:01,820
This time round we'll
build a stronger love.

323
00:21:03,700 --> 00:21:06,297
Oh, you've got me heart and soul.

324
00:21:06,380 --> 00:21:10,897
I just wanna hold you and not let go.

325
00:21:10,980 --> 00:21:15,680
You know that I'll be with
you till the end of time.

326
00:21:19,120 --> 00:21:21,520
Oh, you've got me heart and soul.
